<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tlalmanalco</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tlalmanalco is a town in the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> near the foot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iztaccihuatl">Iztaccíhuatl</a>. It was one of the principal altepetl of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalca">Chalca</a> confederation and its leading political centre after the Aztec conquest. Its 16th-century Franciscan convent, with an elaborately carved open chapel, is one of the finest early colonial buildings in Mexico.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tlalmanalco.jpg" alt="Tlalmanalco" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thelmadatter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SanLuisObispoChurchTlalMX.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
